WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.267
-Today is Friday and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.334
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.267
I check my inbox,
I return some emails,

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.234
and, of course,
I send out thank you notes.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
And I was just --

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.767
I was running a bit behind.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.701
I'd like to read some
thank you notes out right now.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.834
James, can I get some thank you
note-writing music, please?

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:15.767
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:18.200
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.200
Yeah.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:19.968
Good stuff.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.901
-Wow, Mr. Energy.
-Hm.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.567
♪♪

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:24.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:26.334
Thank you, the Oscars,

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.534
for announcing
your nominations this week.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.367
I just feel bad for whoever had
to tell Megan she got snubbed.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.467
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.701
Thank you, trying to make
Valentine's Day reservations,

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.868
for being a slow process
of going from perfect date to

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.267
"Is there a hot dog stand
you like??

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:50.300
-Whoo!

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.200
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.868
Thank you,
CEO of Dollar General,

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.300
for leaving to become CEO
of Dollar Tree.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.400
Or, as the Verizon guy put it,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.701
"Game respect game."

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.334
♪♪

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.000
-Whoo!

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.033
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.901
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.400
Thank you, three different
television remotes

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.701
on my friend's coffee table...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.367
...for letting me know that this
is going to be a whole thing.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Which thing I want?

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.868
Which one?

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.567
Which one is it?
-Oh, let me -- Hold on.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:27.734
Hold on, let me see.
-No, that's not the right one.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.100
-Give me the other one.
-That's not -- no,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.167
you want the Apple remote.
-Hold on.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.901
Give me that one.
-Which one? This one?

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.033
[ Laughter ]
The thin one?
-Wait.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.367
Give me the battery.
Give me the batteries

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.200
from that one.
-Okay.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:38.834
♪♪

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.467
Thank, you wobbly ceiling fans,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.701
for helping cool me down
while I kind of sleep in fear.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:47.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.200
-[ Reverberating ]

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.767
[ Imitating blades whirring ]

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.033
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.067
Thank you, the price of eggs,

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:59.701
for reaching an all-time high.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.434
Or, as Faberge eggs put it,
"Stay in your lane, girl.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.133
[ Laughter ]
Stay. You know.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.033
[ Cheering ]

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.234
I'm the fancy egg.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:10.634
[ Applause ]

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:11.934
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:16.200
Thank you,
49ers mascot Sourdough Sam,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.501
for looking like a nutcracker

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:19.601
whose wife and mistress
just met each other.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.601
[ Cheering ]

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.300
[ Rimshot ]
"You know...?

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.100
Wow!"

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.634
You and Susie know each other?

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.801
[ Laughter ]
What?! That's so funny.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.000
That's so funny."

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.734
♪♪
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.767
Thank you, Dry January,

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.567
or, as it's known
on February 1st,

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:45.000
bye, bish.
There you have it, everybody.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.801
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
Those are our Thank You Notes.

